Add({
	id = "swamp-of-sorrows",
	title = "Swamp of Sorrows",
	aliases = { "the Swamp of Sorrows" },
	faction = "Contested",
	continent = "Eastern Kingdoms",
	maps = { 1435, 51 },
	zone = "Swamp of Sorrows",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
		{ type = "map" },
	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Swamp of Sorrows is a sunken country of black water, hanging moss and endless rain in the south-east of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. It lies east of {link:deadwind-pass}Deadwind Pass{/link} and north of the {link:blasted-lands}Blasted Lands{/link}, and its eastern shore breaks against the Forbidding Sea. Its trees are drowned to the knee, its paths vanish under the mud, and its pools breed crocolisks, great spiders and walking tangles of living weed. No kingdom has ever tamed it. The orcs of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} hold a fortress at its heart, a small company of exiles clings to its western edge, murlocs swarm along its coast, and green dragons keep a silent watch over a lake where a troll temple lies drowned.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records who first named the swamp, or why it was called a place of sorrow. What is remembered is that it has long been a land of exiles. When the Gurubashi trolls cast down their blood god {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link}, they drove his priests, the Atal'ai, out of the jungles of the south. The Atal'ai fled north into these marshes. There they raised a great temple, the {link:temple-of-atal-hakkar}Temple of Atal'Hakkar{/link}, where they meant to call their god back into the world. The green dragonflight of {red:ysera}Ysera{/red} would not allow it. The dragons broke the temple and sank it beneath the waters of the {link:pool-of-tears}Pool of Tears{/link}, and there it lies still. No chronicle gives the year.

South of the swamp lay the Black Morass. It was there that the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened, and from there the orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link} marched out to make war on the kingdom of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} in the {link:first-war}First War{/link}. The swamp was the Horde's first neighbour in this world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The swamp is contested ground. The Warchief {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} keeps the fortress of {link:stonard}Stonard{/link} at its centre, and his orcs have sent envoys to learn what befell the drowned temple. The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} holds no town here. Its caravans only pass through on the long road from {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link} to {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde Keep{/link}, and many of them do not arrive. In the north, a people called the lost ones prey on anyone who wanders near their village. In the west, a band of draenei exiles who share their blood but not their madness hide at the {link:the-harborage}Harborage{/link}. Along the eastern shore, the murlocs grow bolder each season. And over all of it, the green dragons circle and wait, guarding the temple against the day its priests stir again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The orcs of {link:stonard}Stonard{/link}.{/b} Warriors, scouts and traders of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} who hold the swamp's only fortress, and who guard its roads and its coast.
• {b}The draenei of the {link:the-harborage}Harborage{/link}.{/b} A small company of exiles in the west, who came to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} from far away and now fear their own kin.
• {b}The lost ones.{/b} {link:kinelory}Kin{/link} of the draenei, driven mad by the long journey that brought them here. They hold the {link:fallow-sanctuary}Fallow Sanctuary{/link} in the north.
• {b}The green dragonflight.{/b} Whelps, wyrmkin and scalebanes of Ysera's flight guard the {link:pool-of-tears}Pool of Tears{/link} and the lands about it. A dragon named {link:itharius}Itharius{/link} keeps a cave in the south-west.
• {b}Murlocs.{/b} The {link:murlocs}murloc{/link} tribes of the {link:misty-reed-strand}Misty Reed Strand{/link} swarm along the eastern coast.
• {b}The beasts of the marsh.{/b} Sawtooth crocolisks, jaguars, panthers, great spiders and the walking weeds called swampwalkers and tangled horrors.
• {b}The Atal'ai.{/b} The troll priests of {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} still dwell in the sunken temple below the Pool of Tears.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Exile of the Atal'ai.{/b} Cast out by the Gurubashi, the priests of {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} raised their temple in the swamp.
• {b}The Sinking of the Temple.{/b} The green dragonflight shattered the temple and drowned it, so that the blood god could not return through it.
• {b}The {link:first-war}First War{/link}.{/b} The {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened in the Black Morass to the south, and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} first set foot in this world at the swamp's edge.
• {b}The Founding of {link:stonard}Stonard{/link}.{/b} No chronicle records when the orcs raised Stonard. Today it is the Warchief's fortress in the south, fed by a long road of supply from the camp of {link:grom-gol-base-camp}Grom'gol{/link} in {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn Vale{/link}.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The Horde studies the temple, the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} hurries its caravans past, and the dragons wait.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Swamp",
			text = [=[• The {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} has long sought the {link:temple-of-atal-hakkar}Temple of Atal'Hakkar{/link}. An old {link:dwarves}dwarf{/link} of the League flew over the swamp on a gryphon and never found it. It was found only from the ground, drowned beneath the {link:pool-of-tears}Pool of Tears{/link}.
• The draenei call a sacred crystal draenethyst. It is said to come from a place where mountains fly and demons rule. A shaman of the centaurs in {link:desolace}Desolace{/link} once sent for a shard of it from the swamp.
• A courier of the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} once lost a precious essay here. It was written by {link:khadgar}Khadgar{/link} and bound for {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde Keep{/link}, and the walking weeds of the marsh took it from him.
• Scrawled riddles are left for treasure seekers under an old bridge in the west of the swamp, near the road from {link:deadwind-pass}Deadwind Pass{/link}. The riddles speak of a man named Cortello, and they lead across the sea and back again.
• Goblins pay well for dream dust, a glittering powder gathered from the dragon whelps of the swamp.]=],
		},
	},
})

